  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/8fe1d40d-4948-4d59-94de-02ac7c4c88da-image.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 277px;\" /><br />We know that the formula of the distance between two points is,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></math>, now put the values from the above the diagram in the above formula, then the distance between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt><mo>&#8776;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>a</mi></math></p>",
